From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonid Komarianskyi <leonid_komarianskyi@epam.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Feb 2026 14:20:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xen: mapcache: leave first in buckets unmapped

In general, this commit reverts changes introduced by the following
commits: 872cb9cced796e75d4f719c31d70ed5fd629efca xen: mapcache: Fix
unmapping of first entries in buckets

123acd816dccbd358570ec7ab79c5cb2c863780b xen: mapcache: Unmap first
entries in buckets

With such fixes, observed a lot of map/unmap operations during
virtio-blk IO operations. E.g. on Gen5 setup, every unmap takes about
2-3ms, and according to virtio-blk logic every 1MB read/write may
require 80-256 map and unmap operations, which in total takes avarage
150-200ms and as a result drops IO performance to 3-4MB/s. On the other
hand, leaving the first entries in every bucket always unmapped allows
us to reuse the memory and avoid numerious of map/unmaps.

This is a workaround solution, as a proper fix requires debugging the
root cause, why every unmap operation takes a few ms. Note: this is how
it works now in QEMU 7 without any observed issues.

(cherry picked from commit 8e6a6725d07530cbe5051255c25433d7b6841a81)

Signed-off-by: Leonid Komarianskyi <leonid_komarianskyi@epam.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream fork / BSP-layer delta; not submitted upstream]
Origin: https://github.com/xen-troops/qemu commit 8e6a6725d07530cbe5051255c25433d7b6841a81
---
 hw/xen/xen-mapcache.c | 20 +++-----------------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/xen/xen-mapcache.c b/hw/xen/xen-mapcache.c
index 85cf0cf35..6cd5b16c5 100644
--- a/hw/xen/xen-mapcache.c
+++ b/hw/xen/xen-mapcache.c
@@ -597,10 +597,11 @@ static void xen_invalidate_map_cache_entry_unlocked(MapCache *mc,
         return;
     }
     entry->lock--;
-    if (entry->lock > 0) {
+    if (entry->lock > 0 || pentry == NULL) {
         return;
     }
 
+    pentry->next = entry->next;
     ram_block_notify_remove(entry->vaddr_base, entry->size, entry->size);
     if (entry->flags & XEN_MAPCACHE_ENTRY_GRANT) {
         rc = xengnttab_unmap(xen_region_gnttabdev, entry->vaddr_base,
@@ -615,22 +616,7 @@ static void xen_invalidate_map_cache_entry_unlocked(MapCache *mc,
     }
 
     g_free(entry->valid_mapping);
-    if (pentry) {
-        pentry->next = entry->next;
-        g_free(entry);
-    } else {
-        /*
-         * Invalidate mapping but keep entry->next pointing to the rest
-         * of the list.
-         *
-         * Note that lock is already zero here, otherwise we don't unmap.
-         */
-        entry->paddr_index = 0;
-        entry->vaddr_base = NULL;
-        entry->valid_mapping = NULL;
-        entry->flags = 0;
-        entry->size = 0;
-    }
+    g_free(entry);
 }
 
 typedef struct XenMapCacheData {
